ia-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-disabled stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-none stacks:group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:layers-1-accent-layer stacks:group-active/btn:layers-2-fill-button-layer stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:layers-2-fill-button-layer "></span></span><span class="inline-flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1 "><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:533.3" class="text-muted" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></button></div></div></div><span role="status" class="sr-only"></span></div></div><p>This is the reference for prompt engineering with current Claude models, including Claude Fable 5.1, Claude Mythos 5.1, Claude Fable 5, Claude Mythos 5, Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Opus 5, Claude Opus 4.8, Claude Opus 4.7, Claude Opus 4.6, Claude Sonnet 5.5, Claude Sonnet 5, Claude Sonnet 4.6, Claude Haiku 5.5, and Claude Haiku 4.5. The page is organized in three parts:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong><a href="#model-specific-guidance">Model-specific guidance</a></strong> first: where a single model behaves differently and what to change in your prompt.</li>
<li><strong>Techniques for all current models</strong> after that: general principles, output and formatting, tool use, thinking, and agentic systems.</li>
<li><strong>Migration considerations</strong> last, for prompts moving from earlier generations.</li>
</ul>
<aside data-cds="Aside" data-prose-box="" data-icon-layout="first-line" role="note" class="flex items-start gap-xs rounded-card px-lg py-md font-sans text-body font-normal break-words bg-surface-1 layers-1-[color:var(--cds-banner-neutral-tint)] text-primary shadow-[inset_0_0_0_var(--cds-ring-inner)_var(--cds-banner-neutral-ring,var(--cds-ring-color)),0_0_0_var(--cds-ring-outer)_var(--cds-banner-neutral-ring,var(--cds-ring-color))] [--cds-prose-code-color:initial] [--cds-prose-marker-color:var(--cds-text-secondary)] [--cds-text-link-color:initial] prose-block print:break-inside-avoid print:[:is(h2,h3,h4)+&amp;]:break-after-avoid"><span class="flex min-h-[1lh] shrink-0 items-center"><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1.25rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:433.3" aria-hidden="true"></span></span><div class="min-w-0 flex-1"><p>For an overview of model capabilities, see the <a href="/docs/en/models/overview">models overview</a>. For Claude Fable 5.1 capabilities and API changes, see <a href="/docs/en/models/fable-5-1/whats-new-fable-5-1">What’s new in Claude Fable 5.1</a>. For migration guidance, see the <a href="/docs/en/about-claude/models/migration-guide">Migration guide</a>. For Claude Opus 5.5, see <a href="/docs/en/models/opus-5-5/whats-new-opus-5-5">What’s new in Claude Opus 5.5</a>. For Claude Sonnet 5.5, see <a href="/docs/en/models/sonnet-5-5/whats-new-sonnet-5-5">What’s new in Claude Sonnet 5.5</a>. For Claude Haiku 5.5, see <a href="/docs/en/models/haiku-5-5/whats-new-haiku-5-5">What’s new in Claude Haiku 5.5</a>.</p></div></aside>
