oup-hover/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent  stacks:group-hover/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-hover/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:layers-1-accent-layer stacks:group-active/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-active/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer "></span></span><span class="inline-flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1 "><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:533.3" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></button></span></h2>
<p>Each of these models has its own prompting page. Read the one for your model first, then the techniques that follow.</p>
<div class="prose-scroll relative print:overflow-visible"><table><thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Guide</th><th>What’s different</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="">Claude Fable 5.1 and Claude Mythos 5.1</td><td class=""><a href="/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-engineering/prompting-claude-fable-5-1">Prompting Claude Fable 5.1</a></td><td class="">Differences from Claude Fable 5: effort levels, finishing long tasks, user-facing progress updates, passing thinking blocks back unchanged, tool-call batching in agent loops, search triggering at low effort, formatting, and writing density.</td></tr><tr><td class="">Claude Fable 5 and Claude Mythos 5</td><td class=""><a href="/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-engineering/prompting-claude-fable-5">Prompting Claude Fable 5</a></td><td class="">Differences from Claude Opus 4.8: effort levels, instruction following, long-run progress claims, memory systems, and the <code>reasoning_extraction</code> refusal category.</td></tr><tr><td class="docs-nowrap">Claude Sonnet 5.5</td><td class=""><a href="/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-engineering/prompting-claude-sonnet-5-5">Prompting Claude Sonnet 5.5</a></td><td class="">Differences from Claude Sonnet 5: effort calibration, initiative and scope, running without up-front thinking, JSON output on reasoning tasks, user-facing progress updates, tool use in chat, mid-turn user messages, verification on coding tasks, tool-call handling, complex visual inputs, and safeguard refusals.</td></tr><tr><td class="docs-nowrap">Claude Sonnet 5</td><td class=""><a href="/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-engineering/prompting-claude-sonnet-5">Prompting Claude Sonnet 5</a></td><td class="">Differences from Claude Sonnet 4.6: response length, effort and thinking-depth calibration, tool use triggering, literal instruction following, and design and frontend defaults.</td></tr><tr><td class="docs-nowrap">Claude Opus 5.5</td><td class=""><a href="/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-engineering/prompting-claude-opus-5-5">Prompting Claude Opus 5.5</a></td><td class="">Differences from Claude Opus 5: effort calibration, prompts written for thinking disabled, user-facing progress updates, safeguard refusals, and tools for complex visual inputs.</td></tr><tr><td class="docs-nowrap">Claude Opus 5</td><td class=""><a href="/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-engineering/prompting-claude-opus-5">Prompting Claude Opus 5</a></td><td class="">Differences from prior Opus models: response length and verbosity, user-facing progress updates, written deliverable length, task scope and over-verification, subagent control, and self-correction.</td></tr><tr><td class="docs-nowrap">Claude Opus 4.8</td><td class=""><a href="/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-engineering/prompting-claude-opus-4-8">Prompting Claude Opus 4.8</a></td><td class="">Response length, effort and thinking-depth calibration, tool use triggering, literal instruction following, subagent control, and design and frontend defaults.</td></tr><tr><td class="docs-nowrap">Claude Haiku 5.5</td><td class=""><a href="/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-engineering/prompting-claude-haiku-5-5">Prompting Claude Haiku 5.5</a></td><td class="">Differences from Claude Haiku 4.5: effort levels, search, JSON output with your own tools, early stopping in long agent prompts, verification on coding tasks, mid-turn user messages, system prompt adherence in chatbots, and safeguard refusals.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<h2 id="general-principles" class="group">General principles<span class="relative hidden h-[1em] w-0 align-middle lg:inline-block"><span role="status" aria-live="polite" class="sr-only"></span><button type="button" data-cds="Button" data-cds-icon-only="" data-cds-ghost="" data-size="xs" class="cds-reset group/btn isolate inline-flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap select-none cursor-[var(--cds-cursor-interactive)] aria-disabled:cursor-default data-[disabled]:cursor-default border-0 outline-none focus-visible:outline-hidden [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:outline-hidden rounded h-control font-sans text-body [&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-disabled disabled:pointer-events-none transition-shadow duration-fast text-primary font-normal font-control aria-pressed:text-accent focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:shadow-focus aspect-square w-control px-0 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-100 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:text-button-disabled stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:[--cds-shortcut-cap-ink:currentColor] stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:not-in-data-[cds=SplitDropdownButton]:[--cds-text-button-disabled:var(--cds-fizzy-lake-color-icon-only-disabled)] absolute top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 data-[copied]:opacity-100 touch:opacity-100" aria-label="Copy link to General principles" id="_R_183fcqalubtabsknr5td9leailb_" data-base-ui-tooltip-trigger=""><span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute -z-[1] rounded-[inherit] inset-0 cds-btn-squish stacks:transform-none!"><span data-cds-part="paint" class="absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] transition-[background-color,box-shadow,color] stacks:transition-[box-shadow,color] duration-fast ease-out group-focus-visible/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] group-[[data-initial-focus]:focus]/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] bg-transparent group-hover/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent  stacks:group-hover/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-hover/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:layers-1-accent-layer stacks:group-active/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-active/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer "></span></span><span class="inline-flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1 "><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:533.3" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></button></span></h2>
<p>The techniques in this section and the sections that follow apply to current Claude models, including Claude Fable 5.1, Claude Mythos 5.1, Claude Fable 5, and Claude Mythos 5. Where a technique names a specific model, treat it as measured on that model and re-check it against your own evals before applying it to another.</p>
<h3 id="be-clear-and-direct" class="group">Be clear and direct<span class="relative hidden h-[1em] w-0 align-middle lg:inline-block"><span role="status" aria-live="polite" class="sr-only"></span><button type="button" data-cds="Button" data-cds-icon-only="" data-cds-ghost="" data-size="xs" class="cds-reset group/btn isolate inline-flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap select-none cursor-[var(--cds-cursor-interactive)] aria-disabled:cursor-default data-[disabled]:cursor-default border-0 outline-none focus-visible:outline-hidden [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:outline-hidden rounded h-control font-sans text-body [&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-disabled disabled:pointer-events-none transition-shadow duration-fast text-primary font-normal font-control aria-pressed:text-accent focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:shadow-focus aspect-square w-control px-0 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-100 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:text-button-disabled stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:[--cds-shortcut-cap-ink:currentColor] stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:not-in-data-[cds=SplitDropdownButton]:[--cds-text-button-disabled:var(--cds-fizzy-lake-color-icon-only-disabled)] absolute top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 data-[copied]:opacity-100 touch:opacity-100" aria-label="Copy link to Be clear and direct" id="_R_184fcqalubtabsknr5td9leailb_" data-base-ui-tooltip-trigger=""><span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute -z-[1] rounded-[inherit] inset-0 cds-btn-squish stacks:transform-none!"><span data-cds-part="paint" class="absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] transition-[background-color,box-shadow,color] stacks:transition-[box-shadow,color] duration-fast ease-out group-focus-visible/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] group-[[data-initial-focus]:focus]/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] bg-transparent group-hover/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent  stacks:group-hover/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-hover/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:layers-1-accent-layer stacks:group-active/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-active/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer "></span></span><span class="inline-flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1 "><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:533.3" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></button></span></h3>
<p>Claude responds well to clear, explicit instructions. Being specific about the output you want can help enhance results. If you want Claude to do more than the task strictly requires, explicitly request it rather than relying on the model to infer this from vague prompts.</p>
<p>Think of Claude as a brilliant but new employee who lacks context on your norms and workflows. The more precisely you explain what you want, the better the result.</p>
<p><strong>Key test:</strong> Show your prompt to a colleague with minimal context on the task and ask them to follow it. If they’d be confused, Claude will be too.</p>
<ul>
<li>Be specific about the output format and constraints you want.</li>
<li>Provide instructions as sequential steps using numbered lists or bullet points when the order or completeness of steps matters.</li>
</ul>
