<h3 id="improved-vision-capabilities" class="group">Improved vision capabilities<span class="relative hidden h-[1em] w-0 align-middle lg:inline-block"><span role="status" aria-live="polite" class="sr-only"></span><button type="button" data-cds="Button" data-cds-icon-only="" data-cds-ghost="" data-size="xs" class="cds-reset group/btn isolate inline-flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap select-none cursor-[var(--cds-cursor-interactive)] aria-disabled:cursor-default data-[disabled]:cursor-default border-0 outline-none focus-visible:outline-hidden [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:outline-hidden rounded h-control font-sans text-body [&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-disabled disabled:pointer-events-none transition-shadow duration-fast text-primary font-normal font-control aria-pressed:text-accent focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:shadow-focus aspect-square w-control px-0 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-100 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:text-button-disabled stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:[--cds-shortcut-cap-ink:currentColor] stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:not-in-data-[cds=SplitDropdownButton]:[--cds-text-button-disabled:var(--cds-fizzy-lake-color-icon-only-disabled)] absolute top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 data-[copied]:opacity-100 touch:opacity-100" aria-label="Copy link to Improved vision capabilities" id="_R_1abvcqalubtabsknr5td9leailb_" data-base-ui-tooltip-trigger=""><span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute -z-[1] rounded-[inherit] inset-0 cds-btn-squish stacks:transform-none!"><span data-cds-part="paint" class="absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] transition-[background-color,box-shadow,color] stacks:transition-[box-shadow,color] duration-fast ease-out group-focus-visible/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] group-[[data-initial-focus]:focus]/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] bg-transparent group-hover/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent  stacks:group-hover/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-hover/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:layers-1-accent-layer stacks:group-active/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-active/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer "></span></span><span class="inline-flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1 "><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:533.3" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></button></span></h3>
<p>Claude Opus 4.5 and Claude Opus 4.6 have improved vision capabilities compared to previous Claude models. They perform better on image processing and data extraction tasks, particularly when there are multiple images present in context. These improvements carry over to computer use, where the models can more reliably interpret screenshots and UI elements. You can also use these models to analyze videos by breaking them up into frames.</p>
<p>One technique that has proven effective to further boost performance is to give Claude a crop tool or <a href="/docs/en/agents-and-tools/agent-skills/overview">agent skill</a>. Testing has shown consistent uplift on image evaluations when Claude is able to “zoom” in on relevant regions of an image. Anthropic has created a <a href="https://platform.claude.com/cookbook/multimodal-crop-tool" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">recipe for the crop tool</a>.</p>
<h3 id="frontend-design" class="group">Frontend design<span class="relative hidden h-[1em] w-0 align-middle lg:inline-block"><span role="status" aria-live="polite" class="sr-only"></span><button type="button" data-cds="Button" data-cds-icon-only="" data-cds-ghost="" data-size="xs" class="cds-reset group/btn isolate inline-flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap select-none cursor-[var(--cds-cursor-interactive)] aria-disabled:cursor-default data-[disabled]:cursor-default border-0 outline-none focus-visible:outline-hidden [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:outline-hidden rounded h-control font-sans text-body [&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-disabled disabled:pointer-events-none transition-shadow duration-fast text-primary font-normal font-control aria-pressed:text-accent focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:shadow-focus aspect-square w-control px-0 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-100 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:text-button-disabled stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:[--cds-shortcut-cap-ink:currentColor] stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:not-in-data-[cds=SplitDropdownButton]:[--cds-text-button-disabled:var(--cds-fizzy-lake-color-icon-only-disabled)] absolute top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 data-[copied]:opacity-100 touch:opacity-100" aria-label="Copy link to Frontend design" id="_R_1adfcqalubtabsknr5td9leailb_" data-base-ui-tooltip-trigger=""><span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute -z-[1] rounded-[inherit] inset-0 cds-btn-squish stacks:transform-none!"><span data-cds-part="paint" class="absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] transition-[background-color,box-shadow,color] stacks:transition-[box-shadow,color] duration-fast ease-out group-focus-visible/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] group-[[data-initial-focus]:focus]/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] bg-transparent group-hover/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent  stacks:group-hover/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-hover/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:layers-1-accent-layer stacks:group-active/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-active/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer "></span></span><span class="inline-flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1 "><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:533.3" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></button></span></h3>
<p>Claude Opus 4.5 and Claude Opus 4.6 build complex, real-world web applications with strong frontend design. However, without guidance, models can default to generic patterns that create what users call the “AI slop” aesthetic. To create distinctive, creative front ends that surprise and delight:</p>
<aside data-cds="Aside" data-prose-box="" data-icon-layout="first-line" role="note" class="flex items-start gap-xs rounded-card px-lg py-md font-sans text-body font-normal break-words bg-surface-1 layers-1-[color:var(--cds-banner-neutral-tint)] text-primary shadow-[inset_0_0_0_var(--cds-ring-inner)_var(--cds-banner-neutral-ring,var(--cds-ring-color)),0_0_0_var(--cds-ring-outer)_var(--cds-banner-neutral-ring,var(--cds-ring-color))] [--cds-prose-code-color:initial] [--cds-prose-marker-color:var(--cds-text-secondary)] [--cds-text-link-color:initial] prose-block print:break-inside-avoid print:[:is(h2,h3,h4)+&amp;]:break-after-avoid"><span class="flex min-h-[1lh] shrink-0 items-center"><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1.25rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:433.3" aria-hidden="true"></span></span><div class="min-w-0 flex-1"><p>For a detailed guide on improving frontend design, see the blog post on <a href="https://www.claude.com/blog/improving-frontend-design-through-skills" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">improving frontend design through skills</a>.</p></div></aside>
<p>For frontend design work outside the API, <a href="https://support.claude.com/en/articles/14604416-get-started-with-claude-design" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Claude Design</a> provides a canvas and design tools where Claude generates and iterates on designs interactively.</p>
<p>Here’s a system prompt snippet you can use to encourage better frontend design:</p>
<div data-copy-scope="" class="overflow-hidden rounded-card border bg-surface-2 print:[p+&amp;]:break-before-avoid group relative prose-block [&amp;&gt;[data-not-prose]]:mt-0"><div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 border-b px-4 py-1 print:break-after-avoid print:py-sm not-prose"><div class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-2 text-caption text-muted">Sample prompt for frontend aesthetics</div><div class="flex shrink-0 items-center gap-1 print:hidden"><span class="contents group-[:not(:has([data-code-source]))]/codegroup:hidden"><button type="button" data-cds="Button" data-cds-icon-only="" data-cds-ghost="" data-size="sm" class="cds-reset group/btn relative isolate inline-flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap select-none cursor-[var(--cds-cursor-interactive)] aria-disabled:cursor-default data-[disabled]:cursor-default border-0 outline-none focus-visible:outline-hidden [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:outline-hidden rounded h-control font-sans text-body [&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-disabled disabled:pointer-events-none transition-shadow duration-fast font-normal font-control aria-pressed:text-accent focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:shadow-focus aspect-square w-control px-0 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-100 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:text-button-disabled stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:[--cds-shortcut-cap-ink:currentColor] stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:not-in-data-[cds=SplitDropdownButton]:[--cds-text-button-disabled:var(--cds-fizzy-lake-color-icon-only-disabled)] text-muted" aria-label="Copy code" id="_R_f6fvcqalubtabsknr5td9leailb_" data-base-ui-tooltip-trigger=""><span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute -z-[1] rounded-[inherit] inset-0 cds-btn-squish stacks:transform-none!"><span data-cds-part="paint" class="absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] transition-[background-color,box-shadow,color] stacks:transition-[box-shadow,color] duration-fast ease-out group-focus-visible/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] group-[[data-initial-focus]:focus]/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] bg-transparent group-hover/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent  stacks:group-hover/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-hover/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:layers-1-accent-layer stacks:group-active/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-active/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer "></span></span><span class="inline-flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1 "><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1.25rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:433.3" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></button><span role="status" class="sr-only"></span></span></div></div><div data-not-prose="true" class="relative h-full py-4 pl-4 text-code code-block-wrap"><div class="block w-full pr-4" data-code-source="" translate="no"><pre class="shiki"><code><span class="line">&lt;frontend_aesthetics&gt;</span>
<span class="line">You tend to converge toward generic, "on distribution" outputs. In frontend design, this</span>
<span class="line">creates what users call the "AI slop" aesthetic. Avoid this: make creative, distinctive</span>
<span class="line">frontends that surprise and delight.</span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line">Focus on:</span>
<span class="line">- Typography: Choose fonts that are beautiful, unique, and interesting. Avoid generic</span>
<span class="line">fonts like Arial and Inter; opt instead for distinctive choices that elevate the</span>
<span class="line">frontend's aesthetics.</span>
<span class="line">- Color &amp; Theme: Commit to a cohesive aesthetic. Use CSS variables for consistency.</span>
<span class="line">Dominant colors with sharp accents outperform timid, <span class="nowrap">evenly-distributed</span> palettes. Draw</span>
<span class="line">from IDE themes and cultural aesthetics for inspiration.</span>
<span class="line">- Motion: Use animations for effects and <span class="nowrap">micro-interactions.</span> Prioritize <span class="nowrap">CSS-only</span></span>
<span class="line">solutions for HTML. Use Motion library for React when available. Focus on <span class="nowrap">high-impact</span></span>
<span class="line">moments: one <span class="nowrap">well-orchestrated</span> page load with staggered reveals <span class="nowrap">(animation-delay)</span></span>
<span class="line">creates more delight than scattered <span class="nowrap">micro-interactions.</span></span>
<span class="line">- Backgrounds: Create atmosphere and depth rather than defaulting to solid colors. Layer</span>
<span class="line">CSS gradients, use geometric patterns, or add contextual effects that match the overall</span>
<span class="line">aesthetic.</span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line">Avoid generic <span class="nowrap">AI-generated</span> aesthetics:</span>
<span class="line">- Overused font families (Inter, Roboto, Arial, system fonts)</span>
<span class="line">- Clichéd color schemes (particularly purple gradients on white backgrounds)</span>
<span class="line">- Predictable layouts and component patterns</span>
<span class="line">- <span class="nowrap">Cookie-cutter</span> design that lacks <span class="nowrap">context-specific</span> character</span>
<span class="line"></span>
<span class="line">Interpret creatively and make unexpected choices that feel genuinely designed for the</span>
<span class="line">context. Vary between light and dark themes, different fonts, different aesthetics. You</span>
<span class="line">still tend to converge on common choices (Space Grotesk, for example) across</span>
<span class="line">generations. Avoid this: it is critical that you think outside the box!</span>
<span class="line">&lt;/frontend_aesthetics&gt;</span></code></pre></div></div></div>
<p>You can also refer to the <a href="https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/blob/main/plugins/frontend-design/skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">full skill definition</a>.</p>
<!-- -->
<h3 id="medication-dosing" class="group">Medication dosing<span class="relative hidden h-[1em] w-0 align-middle lg:inline-block"><span role="status" aria-live="polite" class="sr-only"></span><button type="button" data-cds="Button" data-cds-icon-only="" data-cds-ghost="" data-size="xs" class="cds-reset group/btn isolate inline-flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap select-none cursor-[var(--cds-cursor-interactive)] aria-disabled:cursor-default data-[disabled]:cursor-default border-0 outline-none focus-visible:outline-hidden [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:outline-hidden rounded h-control font-sans text-body [&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-disabled disabled:pointer-events-none transition-shadow duration-fast text-primary font-normal font-control aria-pressed:text-accent focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:shadow-focus aspect-square w-control px-0 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-100 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:text-button-disabled stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:[--cds-shortcut-cap-ink:currentColor] stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:not-in-data-[cds=SplitDropdownButton]:[--cds-text-button-disabled:var(--cds-fizzy-lake-color-icon-only-disabled)] absolute top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 data-[copied]:opacity-100 touch:opacity-100" aria-label="Copy link to Medication dosing" id="_R_1ah7cqalubtabsknr5td9leailb_" data-base-ui-tooltip-trigger=""><span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute -z-[1] rounded-[inherit] inset-0 cds-btn-squish stacks:transform-none!"><span data-cds-part="paint" class="absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] transition-[background-color,box-shadow,color] stacks:transition-[box-shadow,color] duration-fast ease-out group-focus-visible/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] group-[[data-initial-focus]:focus]/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] bg-transparent group-hover/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent  stacks:group-hover/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-hover/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:layers-1-accent-layer stacks:group-active/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-active/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer "></span></span><span class="inline-flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1 "><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:533.3" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></button></span></h3>
<p>If people might ask your application about medicine doses, add the block below for the model your application calls to your system prompt, exactly as written. The block has Claude give a child’s dose of an over-the-counter medicine from the product’s label, not from memory. With web search, such as the <a href="/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/web-search-tool">web search tool</a>, Claude checks the label before answering, which adds latency and search costs. Without web search, Claude points the person to the label’s dosing chart, a pharmacist, or the child’s doctor instead of giving a dose.</p>
<div data-copy-scope="" class="overflow-hidden rounded-card border bg-surface-2 print:[p+&amp;]:break-before-avoid group relative prose-block [&amp;&gt;[data-not-prose]]:mt-0"><div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 border-b px-4 py-1 print:break-after-avoid print:py-sm not-prose"><div class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-2 text-caption text-muted">Medication dosing block for Claude Fable 5.1, Claude Fable 5, Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Opus 5, Claude Opus 4.8, Claude Opus 4.7, Claude Opus 4.6, Claude Sonnet 5.5, and Claude Sonnet 5</div><div class="flex shrink-0 items-center gap-1 print:hidden"><span class="contents group-[:not(:has([data-code-source]))]/codegroup:hidden"><button type="button" data-cds="Button" data-cds-icon-only="" data-cds-ghost="" data-size="sm" class="cds-reset group/btn relative isolate inline-flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap select-none cursor-[var(--cds-cursor-interactive)] aria-disabled:cursor-default data-[disabled]:cursor-default border-0 outline-none focus-visible:outline-hidden [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:outline-hidden rounded h-control font-sans text-body [&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-disabled disabled:pointer-events-none transition-shadow duration-fast font-normal font-control aria-pressed:text-accent focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:shadow-focus aspect-square w-control px-0 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-100 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:text-button-disabled stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:[--cds-shortcut-cap-ink:currentColor] stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:not-in-data-[cds=SplitDropdownButton]:[--cds-text-button-disabled:var(--cds-fizzy-lake-color-icon-only-disabled)] text-muted" aria-label="Copy code" id="_R_f6i7cqalubtabsknr5td9leailb_" data-base-ui-tooltip-trigger=""><span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute -z-[1] rounded-[inherit] inset-0 cds-btn-squish stacks:transform-none!"><span data-cds-part="paint" class="absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] transition-[background-color,box-shadow,color] stacks:transition-[box-shadow,color] duration-fast ease-out group-focus-visible/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] group-[[data-initial-focus]:focus]/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] bg-transparent group-hover/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent  stacks:group-hover/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-hover/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:layers-1-accent-layer stacks:group-active/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-active/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer "></span></span><span class="inline-flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1 "><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1.25rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:433.3" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></button><span role="status" class="sr-only"></span></span></div></div><div data-not-prose="true" class="relative h-full py-4 pl-4 text-code code-block-wrap"><div class="block w-full pr-4" data-code-source="" translate="no"><pre class="shiki"><code><span class="line">&lt;medical_guidance&gt;</span>
<span class="line">This applies only when the person explicitly says the medicine is for a child, and isn't a healthcare professional asking for work.</span>
<span class="line">Dosing for children's <span class="nowrap">over-the-counter</span> medicines depends on the child's weight and the specific product. For infants and toddlers, a small error can cause real harm. The product's label is the most reliable source, so Claude reports accurately what it says.</span>
<span class="line">If neither the child's age or weight is given, Claude asks for both. If a doctor has prescribed the medicine, Claude defers to the dose on the prescription label and suggests the pharmacist for any questions about it.</span>
<span class="line">If web search is available, Claude uses it to find the product's label and confirms it against an official copy of the same label, such as DailyMed. If web search is not available or Claude can't find the label, Claude doesn't give a number from memory and instead points the person to the label's dosing chart, a pharmacist, or the child's doctor. Claude shares what the label states for the child's age and weight: the dose, plus any instruction to ask a doctor. If the label gives no dose for that age or weight, or says not to use the product, Claude says so and refers the person to their doctor or pharmacist.</span>
<span class="line">&lt;/medical_guidance&gt;</span></code></pre></div></div></div>
<div data-copy-scope="" class="overflow-hidden rounded-card border bg-surface-2 print:[p+&amp;]:break-before-avoid group relative prose-block [&amp;&gt;[data-not-prose]]:mt-0"><div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 border-b px-4 py-1 print:break-after-avoid print:py-sm not-prose"><div class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-2 text-caption text-muted">Medication dosing block for Claude Haiku 5.5</div><div class="flex shrink-0 items-center gap-1 print:hidden"><span class="contents group-[:not(:has([data-code-source]))]/codegroup:hidden"><button type="button" data-cds="Button" data-cds-icon-only="" data-cds-ghost="" data-size="sm" class="cds-reset group/btn relative isolate inline-flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap select-none cursor-[var(--cds-cursor-interactive)] aria-disabled:cursor-default data-[disabled]:cursor-default border-0 outline-none focus-visible:outline-hidden [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:outline-hidden rounded h-control font-sans text-body [&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-disabled disabled:pointer-events-none transition-shadow duration-fast font-normal font-control aria-pressed:text-accent focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:shadow-focus aspect-square w-control px-0 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-100 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:text-button-disabled stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:[--cds-shortcut-cap-ink:currentColor] stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:not-in-data-[cds=SplitDropdownButton]:[--cds-text-button-disabled:var(--cds-fizzy-lake-color-icon-only-disabled)] text-muted" aria-label="Copy code" id="_R_f6incqalubtabsknr5td9leailb_" data-base-ui-tooltip-trigger=""><span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute -z-[1] rounded-[inherit] inset-0 cds-btn-squish stacks:transform-none!"><span data-cds-part="paint" class="absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] transition-[background-color,box-shadow,color] stacks:transition-[box-shadow,color] duration-fast ease-out group-focus-visible/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] group-[[data-initial-focus]:focus]/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] bg-transparent group-hover/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent  stacks:group-hover/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-hover/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:layers-1-accent-layer stacks:group-active/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-active/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer "></span></span><span class="inline-flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1 "><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1.25rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:433.3" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></button><span role="status" class="sr-only"></span></span></div></div><div data-not-prose="true" class="relative h-full py-4 pl-4 text-code code-block-wrap"><div class="block w-full pr-4" data-code-source="" translate="no"><pre class="shiki"><code><span class="line">&lt;medical_guidance&gt;</span>
<span class="line">This applies only when the person explicitly says the medicine is for a child, and isn't a healthcare professional asking for work.</span>
<span class="line">Dosing for children's <span class="nowrap">over-the-counter</span> medicines depends on the child's age or weight and the specific product. For infants and toddlers, a small error can cause real harm. The product's label is the most reliable source, so Claude reports accurately what it says.</span>
<span class="line">If neither the child's age or weight is given, Claude asks for both. If a doctor has prescribed the medicine, Claude defers to the dose on the prescription label and suggests the pharmacist for any questions about it.</span>
<span class="line">If web search is available, Claude uses it to find the product's label and confirms it against an official copy of the same label, such as DailyMed. If web search is not available or Claude can't find the label, Claude doesn't give a number from memory and instead points the person to the label's dosing chart, a pharmacist, or the child's doctor. Claude shares what the label states for the child's age or weight: the dose, plus any instruction to ask a doctor. If the label gives no dose for that age or weight, or says not to use the product, Claude says so and refers the person to their doctor or pharmacist.</span>
<span class="line">If someone mentions emotional distress or a difficult experience and asks about a medication's dose or limit, Claude should not provide the requested information and should instead address the underlying emotional distress.</span>
<span class="line">&lt;/medical_guidance&gt;</span></code></pre></div></div></div>
<div data-copy-scope="" class="overflow-hidden rounded-card border bg-surface-2 print:[p+&amp;]:break-before-avoid group relative prose-block [&amp;&gt;[data-not-prose]]:mt-0"><div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 border-b px-4 py-1 print:break-after-avoid print:py-sm not-prose"><div class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-2 text-caption text-muted">Medication dosing block for Claude Sonnet 4.6</div><div class="flex shrink-0 items-center gap-1 print:hidden"><span class="contents group-[:not(:has([data-code-source]))]/codegroup:hidden"><button type="button" data-cds="Button" data-cds-icon-only="" data-cds-ghost="" data-size="sm" class="cds-reset group/btn relative isolate inline-flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap select-none cursor-[var(--cds-cursor-interactive)] aria-disabled:cursor-default data-[disabled]:cursor-default border-0 outline-none focus-visible:outline-hidden [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:outline-hidden rounded h-control font-sans text-body [&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-disabled disabled:pointer-events-none transition-shadow duration-fast font-normal font-control aria-pressed:text-accent focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:shadow-focus aspect-square w-control px-0 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-100 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:text-button-disabled stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:[--cds-shortcut-cap-ink:currentColor] stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:not-in-data-[cds=SplitDropdownButton]:[--cds-text-button-disabled:var(--cds-fizzy-lake-color-icon-only-disabled)] text-muted" aria-label="Copy code" id="_R_f6j7cqalubtabsknr5td9leailb_" data-base-ui-tooltip-trigger=""><span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute -z-[1] rounded-[inherit] inset-0 cds-btn-squish stacks:transform-none!"><span data-cds-part="paint" class="absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] transition-[background-color,box-shadow,color] stacks:transition-[box-shadow,color] duration-fast ease-out group-focus-visible/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] group-[[data-initial-focus]:focus]/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] bg-transparent group-hover/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent  stacks:group-hover/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-hover/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:layers-1-accent-layer stacks:group-active/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-active/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer "></span></span><span class="inline-flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1 "><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1.25rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:433.3" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></button><span role="status" class="sr-only"></span></span></div></div><div data-not-prose="true" class="relative h-full py-4 pl-4 text-code code-block-wrap"><pre class="block w-full pr-4" data-code-source="" translate="no"><code>&lt;medical_guidance&gt;
If web search is available, Claude uses it to find the children&#x27;s medicine label and confirms it against an official copy of the same label, such as DailyMed. Claude takes a child&#x27;s dose only from the product&#x27;s label, either an official copy found with web search or one shared by the person. Unless that label is in this conversation, Claude doesn&#x27;t state any amount, dose, dosing table, or typical range for a child, including numbers it remembers or works out from the child&#x27;s weight. Without the label, Claude points the person to a pharmacist or the child&#x27;s doctor.
This applies only to medicine the person explicitly says will be given to a child and not to healthcare professionals asking for work.
If a doctor has prescribed the medicine, Claude defers to the dose on the prescription label and suggests the pharmacist for any questions about it.
If neither the child&#x27;s age nor weight is given, Claude asks for both.
Claude shares what the label states for the child&#x27;s age or weight: the dose, plus any instruction to ask a doctor. If the label gives no dose for that age or weight, or says not to use the product, Claude says so and refers the person to their doctor or pharmacist.
&lt;/medical_guidance&gt;</code></pre></div></div>
<div data-copy-scope="" class="overflow-hidden rounded-card border bg-surface-2 print:[p+&amp;]:break-before-avoid group relative prose-block [&amp;&gt;[data-not-prose]]:mt-0"><div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 border-b px-4 py-1 print:break-after-avoid print:py-sm not-prose"><div class="flex min-w-0 items-center gap-2 text-caption text-muted">Medication dosing block for Claude Haiku 4.5</div><div class="flex shrink-0 items-center gap-1 print:hidden"><span class="contents group-[:not(:has([data-code-source]))]/codegroup:hidden"><button type="button" data-cds="Button" data-cds-icon-only="" data-cds-ghost="" data-size="sm" class="cds-reset group/btn relative isolate inline-flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap select-none cursor-[var(--cds-cursor-interactive)] aria-disabled:cursor-default data-[disabled]:cursor-default border-0 outline-none focus-visible:outline-hidden [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:outline-hidden rounded h-control font-sans text-body [&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-disabled disabled:pointer-events-none transition-shadow duration-fast font-normal font-control aria-pressed:text-accent focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:shadow-focus aspect-square w-control px-0 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-100 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:text-button-disabled stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:[--cds-shortcut-cap-ink:currentColor] stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:not-in-data-[cds=SplitDropdownButton]:[--cds-text-button-disabled:var(--cds-fizzy-lake-color-icon-only-disabled)] text-muted" aria-label="Copy code" id="_R_f6jncqalubtabsknr5td9leailb_" data-base-ui-tooltip-trigger=""><span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute -z-[1] rounded-[inherit] inset-0 cds-btn-squish stacks:transform-none!"><span data-cds-part="paint" class="absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] transition-[background-color,box-shadow,color] stacks:transition-[box-shadow,color] duration-fast ease-out group-focus-visible/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] group-[[data-initial-focus]:focus]/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] bg-transparent group-hover/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent  stacks:group-hover/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-hover/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:layers-1-accent-layer stacks:group-active/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-active/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer "></span></span><span class="inline-flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1 "><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1.25rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:433.3" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></button><span role="status" class="sr-only"></span></span></div></div><div data-not-prose="true" class="relative h-full py-4 pl-4 text-code code-block-wrap"><pre class="block w-full pr-4" data-code-source="" translate="no"><code>&lt;medical_guidance&gt;
When someone asks about a medicine for a child and web search is available, Claude uses it to find that medicine&#x27;s label and confirms it against an official copy, such as DailyMed.
When a medicine is for a child, Claude takes the dose only from the product&#x27;s label, either an official copy found with web search or one shared by the person. Unless that label is in this conversation, Claude doesn&#x27;t state any amount, dose, dosing table, or typical range for a child, including numbers it remembers or works out from the child&#x27;s weight. Without the label, Claude points the person to a pharmacist or the child&#x27;s doctor.
Claude gives adults asking about their own medicine the standard dose as usual.
If no child is mentioned, Claude answers as it would for an adult.
If a doctor has prescribed the medicine for a child, Claude doesn&#x27;t look up or work out a dose, even from the product&#x27;s label or the child&#x27;s weight; it defers to the prescription label and suggests the pharmacist for any questions about it.
If neither the child&#x27;s age nor weight is given, Claude asks for both.
Claude shares what the label states for the child&#x27;s age or weight: the dose, plus any instruction to ask a doctor. If the child&#x27;s age or weight is above or below what the label&#x27;s chart includes, or the label says not to use the product, Claude says so and refers the person to their doctor or pharmacist. Claude doesn&#x27;t give doses from charts other than the product&#x27;s label.
&lt;/medical_guidance&gt;</code></pre></div></div>
<h2 id="migration-considerations" class="group">Migration considerations<span class="relative hidden h-[1em] w-0 align-middle lg:inline-block"><span role="status" aria-live="polite" class="sr-only"></span><button type="button" data-cds="Button" data-cds-icon-only="" data-cds-ghost="" data-size="xs" class="cds-reset group/btn isolate inline-flex shrink-0 items-center justify-center gap-1.5 whitespace-nowrap select-none cursor-[var(--cds-cursor-interactive)] aria-disabled:cursor-default data-[disabled]:cursor-default border-0 outline-none focus-visible:outline-hidden [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:outline-hidden rounded h-control font-sans text-body [&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-disabled disabled:pointer-events-none transition-shadow duration-fast text-primary font-normal font-control aria-pressed:text-accent focus-visible:shadow-focus [&amp;[data-initial-focus]:focus]:shadow-focus aspect-square w-control px-0 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:opacity-100 stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:text-button-disabled stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:[--cds-shortcut-cap-ink:currentColor] stacks:[&amp;:disabled:not([aria-busy])]:not-in-data-[cds=SplitDropdownButton]:[--cds-text-button-disabled:var(--cds-fizzy-lake-color-icon-only-disabled)] absolute top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100 data-[copied]:opacity-100 touch:opacity-100" aria-label="Copy link to Migration considerations" id="_R_1ak7cqalubtabsknr5td9leailb_" data-base-ui-tooltip-trigger=""><span aria-hidden="true" class="absolute -z-[1] rounded-[inherit] inset-0 cds-btn-squish stacks:transform-none!"><span data-cds-part="paint" class="absolute inset-0 rounded-[inherit] transition-[background-color,box-shadow,color] stacks:transition-[box-shadow,color] duration-fast ease-out group-focus-visible/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] group-[[data-initial-focus]:focus]/btn:shadow-[inset_0_0_0_1px_var(--cds-page-bg)] bg-transparent group-hover/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-ghost-hover group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:bg-accent  stacks:group-hover/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-hover/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-[:disabled:not([aria-busy])]/btn:group-[[aria-haspopup][aria-expanded=true]]/btn:bg-transparent stacks:group-hover/btn:group-aria-pressed/btn:layers-1-accent-layer stacks:group-active/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:bg-fill-button-ghost-hover stacks:group-active/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer stacks:group-has-[:active]/btn:layers-1-fill-button-layer "></span></span><span class="inline-flex min-w-0 items-center gap-1 "><span data-cds="Icon" style="font-size:calc(1rem * var(--cds-rem-scale, 1));font-weight:533.3" aria-hidden="true"></span></span></button></span></h2>
<p>When migrating to current Claude models from earlier generations:</p>
<ol>
<li>
<p><strong>Be specific about the behavior you want:</strong> Consider describing exactly what you’d like to see in the output.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Frame your instructions with modifiers:</strong> Adding modifiers that encourage Claude to increase the quality and detail of its output can help better shape Claude’s performance. For example, instead of “Create an analytics dashboard,” use “Create an analytics dashboard. Include as many relevant features and interactions as possible. Go beyond the basics to create a fully-featured implementation.”</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Request specific features explicitly:</strong> Ask explicitly for animations and interactive elements when you want them.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Update thinking configuration:</strong> Claude 4.6 and later models use <a href="/docs/en/build-with-claude/thinking">adaptive thinking</a> (<code>thinking: {type: &quot;adaptive&quot;}</code>) instead of manual thinking with <code>budget_tokens</code>. On Claude 4.7 and later models, setting <code>budget_tokens</code> returns a 400 error. Use the <a href="/docs/en/build-with-claude/effort">effort parameter</a> to control thinking depth.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Migrate away from prefilled responses:</strong> Prefilled responses on the last assistant turn are no longer supported starting with Claude 4.6 models and Claude Mythos Preview. See <a href="#migrating-away-from-prefilled-responses">Migrating away from prefilled responses</a> for detailed guidance on alternatives.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Tune anti-laziness prompting:</strong> If your prompts previously encouraged the model to be more thorough or use tools more aggressively, reduce that guidance. Claude 4.6 models are more proactive and might overtrigger on instructions that were needed for previous models.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Pass thinking blocks back unchanged and keep history append-only:</strong> Append each assistant turn exactly as the API returned it, thinking blocks included. On Claude 5.1 and later models, editing earlier messages, rebuilding <code>system</code> or <code>tools</code>, or summarizing older turns in place between requests <a href="/docs/en/build-with-claude/thinking#preserved-in-conversation">invalidates every later thinking block</a>. Move those changes to mid-conversation system messages and server-side context management. See <a href="/docs/en/build-with-claude/prompt-engineering/prompting-claude-fable-5-1#keep-the-conversation-history-append-only">Keep the conversation history append-only</a>.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p>For detailed migration steps, see the <a href="/docs/en/about-claude/models/migration-guide">Migration guide</a>.</p>
